findings.description:
T13 says to reuse 320's existing result-discovery surface. `capture.py` has only `resolve_target` and `_candidates_by_type`, which resolve one target by index or type. Nothing enumerates every judge review under `project-documents/user/reviews`. The fallback is to "scope to the store-recorded samples only", and that cannot produce unsampled offers. Store samples are exactly the already-sampled results.

The core of the slice is therefore unplanned. A real task needs:
- a review-dir walk;
- a `derive_judge_config_id` and `derive_artifact_level` call per file;
- a sampled test, which is under-specified because `SampleVerdict.result_ref` is `(project_id, relative path, content_hash)` and review files are overwritten on re-run, so "not sampled" must say whether it matches on path, on hash, or on both, and which project;
- a rule for the case where a file is unreadable.

The "ask the Project Manager" step blocks a junior. Settle it in the plan instead.

T14's pruned-file case is also incoherent with this design. Discovery scans files that exist, so nothing references a deleted file. The "skip and count" row from the slice's failure table has no defined trigger.
